      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T04:51:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think mocking this in this way is difficult to understand because it overrides all interfaces used by getUidStatsForTransport, and it\u0027s very implementation-dependent.\n\nYour test is already calling `mService.notifyNetworkStatus`. I think this should fill in the necessary interfaces that the service thinks it saw. The only thing you\u0027d need to do is make sure that augmentWithStackedInterfaces doesn\u0027t change them.\n\nThe best way to do this would be to call the real method, unfortunately you don\u0027t have an object to call the real method. So instead, one thing you could do that makes sense is to just say that augmentWithStackedInterfaces always returns the list of ifaces that were passed. You could do this with something like :\n\n    doAnwser(inv -\u003e inv.getArgument(0))\n            .when(mStatFactory).augmentWithStackedIntefaces(any()));\n\n...or if you need a copy (the real method returns a copy)\n\n    doAnswer(inv -\u003e inv.getArgument(0).clone())\n            .when(mStatFactory).augmentWithStackedIntefaces(any()));\n\nAn advantage is that you can do this in setup(), and future users of this test will be less surprised by the behavior. WDYT ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2227,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 2227,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "2b093d537a8178434469d9705cdf8b0a8f6b4ea3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
